{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:b1b5475b199d7ef419411c52eedb2a5dce46d01c23f9dba51cc346a0454b3a0c","title":"How does a finite warped compactification restrict the radial range of a brane inflaton? The relevant geometric input is the throat contribution to the full volume that determines the reduced Planck mass.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b106508a6bbba412e38872c27eb6759b42efeddf012b684081be6f8fd64027ee","title":"Can a regular positive-kinetic background evolve through the NEC boundary? The proposed obstruction is quantum excitation near singular acoustic geometry, extending earlier cosmological arguments.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b12282d5e8a48d56d7549c6e40bb5c07ca78aa244bfdf12d3729698627d8b935","title":"Do U(1)^496 and E8×U(1)^248 ten-dimensional supergravities possess quantum-gravity completions? The paper tests requirements on compactification moduli spaces and on the fate of supersymmetric naked singularities, without assuming a string construction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1c1ca76b1114639b8d86b9753df0d93a282aa071324847aa670d9b5d794d0c0","title":"How does vacuum decay change the meaning of metastability in AdS, and what bulk observables could an approximate boundary field theory describe? The paper also asks whether these issues affect eternal-inflation measures.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0009"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1fe9fa868ed404e739a05085de079705a67294001a39ba4bd455a2749f1e928","title":"How do boundary conditions and asymptotic symmetries define conserved charges in asymptotically locally AdS gravity, how 