irectional coverage of charge-to-mass space. One superextremal state need not allow discharge in every direction, so the multicharge conjecture constrains a convex hull rather than a single charge norm.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1cf19af5cf136fbb49041ad43db6f95143cad70f3ae72000c29746dd813c79a","title":"What prevents a tiny change of a large supersymmetry-breaking contribution from raising a tuned quintessence potential into a positive, excessively flat regime? The question concerns correlations among microscopic parameters and the response of stabilized fields.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1558a3a2b93e575c95be3abca4afa24fab0f26b6ac9407516a926c2419a0228","title":"Do the evaporation conclusions survive replacement of exact positive vacuum energy by a very slowly rolling scalar?","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1436282578a1e534304b621ab444ddce67a862fa1ce18817702b89f2f4f2940","title":"Can an explicit smooth dual geometry exhibit a stringy heterotic NS5 instanton contribution without relying on additional zero-mode lifting? The selected examples vary the discrete twist t over a P2 base.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1c93fc5bd729f0a924b625ac241a025e831539fafa556ac661337f9c460e769","title":"Can DS/dS entanglement consistently constrain matter, and what boundary interpretation describes the equal-entropy family of bulk surfaces?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b17b192cb7332f626666e2403428f32350eb275b8babc81be417a62e51a1b956","title":"Can the requirement that a gauge interaction be physically distinguishable from a global symmetry impose a minimum coupling when an EFT has related ultraviolet and infrared cutoffs? How do entropy, black-hole exclusion and the number of degrees of freedom affect that bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1dff6825d7bfdc0ee431f8ceca88c8621c389506485ca8a65988776ab3b6111","title":"Which anomaly tests are required when spacetime or brane topology can fluctuate?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1e9885279f05dd786436917c90c7d04df67b69c3a59b3f950e176c71bf9e2a3","title":"Which fields and cohomology sectors enter the flux-stabilization problem? The paper retains the axio-dilaton and orientifold-odd complex-structure sector of a Type IIB O3/O7 compactification.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b15444e3f748e28f69c21a9110cd54e9f74a2fd6f3689926c2d3bcd8a3d212bf","title":"How can large-charge methods determine the leading-N O(2N) φ⁴ phase diagram, and what do effective-potential convexity and charged-operator dimensions imply about stability and UV completion in 2<D<4 and 4<D<6?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1791e363f5bc022f78eac5dc5fa84301f00499da68bdd36cf9ef5da9f0a9497","title":"How can cosmological gamma-ray propagation constrain extragalactic background light, cosmic star formation, the cosmological distance scale, intergalactic magnetism, photon-ALP coupling and Lorentz-invariance violation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b18796fd6431a2e70b145190a9f2eaeedecac7c459456895518421d6b932858f","title":"Can late-time dark energy EFTs raise cosmologically inferred H0 relative to flat ΛCDM, and which features of the evolving equation of state control that displacement? The study extends perturbative Quintessence analysis to selected Horndeski models.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b140096b3790078111aee96e85ebc49cbf35c6d9cced57bad8fdbb7dd89f2242","title":"Can nonlinear structure observables distinguish a subdominant light massive relic component from ΛCDM with matched linear σ8, and distinguish relic velocity distributions that give the same linear predictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1815e733e5816d59225b9844f227c4539d9efe9e4c8bb9061fa5652500ff444","title":"Can genus-zero Gopakumar–Vafa (GV) invariants reconstruct Kähler moduli spaces, including non-toric phases and Weyl identifications, and provide explicit tests of the lattice WGC in a BPS charge region?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0079"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b14eabbea3d42077605448698eef39b035a7320656a7c2d611221424aa3ab7ca","title":"Can canonical slow-roll inflation with a rescaled Einstein-Hilbert term and, separately, Gauss-Bonnet or Chern-Simons corrections satisfy the paper's Swampland tests and historical Planck constraints, possibly with a blue tensor tilt?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b1d7bab9a6786ac1039c37cf02d276163cf6bc0de359d550177a0ef6411242bc","title":"Can VECRO formation, interpreted as a quantum response of the vacuum to contraction, prevent a Big Crunch and produce a nonsingular cosmological bounce within effective Einstein gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{